; A plain group referenced through a TRANSPARENT ALIAS as a homogeneous-array ELEMENT is refused at
; both the rule-level spelling (`a = [* kv_alias]`) and the member-position one
; (`t = [ x: [* kv_alias] ]`). RFC 8610 repeats the resolved group's members FLAT; the available
; homogeneous carrier would instead serialize every value as a nested array. Resolving the alias is
; therefore necessary for the refusal too — it must not revive the older exit-0 emission of
; `pub type A = Vec<KvAlias>;` / `pub type KvAlias = Kv;` with no emitted `Kv` definition.
; The supported spelling gives the group a one-item TYPE first (`item = [kv_alias]`), then repeats
; that wrapper (`[* item]`). Exact-one array-record splices remain supported separately.
kv = (a: uint, b: uint)
kv_alias = kv
a = [* kv_alias]
t = [ x: [* kv_alias] ]
